{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>You shall not murder.</b> With your hand or with your tongue — to testify against him falsely to put him to death, or by being a talebearer, or by giving bad advice willfully, knowing that he will be killed, or if a secret was revealed to you by which you could save him from death if you reveal it to him, and if you did not reveal it — you are like a murderer:" "<b>You shall not commit adultery.</b> Many thought that adultery means only with a married woman, because they found ינאף את אשת רעהו (Leviticus 20:10), for what reason to say this after it said אשר ינאף את אשת איש (ibid.)? But the interpretation is not as they thought. Now above it is written אשר יקלל את אביו ואת אמו מות יומת, אביו ואמו קלל דמיו בו (ibid. v. 9), and the reason is that he committed a great transgression, for he cursed the parents who gave him birth. Likewise אשר ינאף את אשת רעהו — to declare that he committed a great abomination by committing adultery with the wife of his fellow, and he is obligated to love his fellow as himself. The word נאוף is like זנות, and behold it is written ותנאף את האבן ואת העץ (Jeremiah 3:9). Rav Saadia the Gaon [Saadia] said: it is not fitting to publicize this abomination. For illicit relations are on many levels, and that which is on the lightest level is relations with a virgin or a widow; and above that, a man with his wife when she is a menstruant, for after a few days she is permitted to him; and above this, a married woman, for it is possible her husband dies and she is permitted to him; and above that, a Canaanite woman who is not under the Torah of Israel if he has not given her seed, for she may convert and he may marry her as a wife — only if he has given her seed, he is serving idolatry in itself; and above that, relations with a male, which has no time of permission ever; and above that, that which is outside the species, as if a man lies with an animal. And the Gaon knew the division, for over all the forbidden relations the punishment of extirpation is stated in the section of Acharei Mot, and he left out from this division the mother and the sister and the daughter:" "<b>You shall not steal.</b> It denotes theft, taking money in secret. And there is a thief who is liable to death, such as one who kidnaps a person from Israel, whether he is a minor or lacking in speech. And theft of money — whether in his presence or not in his presence, or whether he deceived him in calculation, or in measure, or in weight. And this word also includes one who steals the heart of another, as Absalom did:" "<b>You shall not testify.</b> For many years I searched in my heart for the reason of this word, to say עד שקר and not עדות שקר. And according to my understanding now, it addresses a false witness, as if written: you shall not testify if you are a false witness. And this word carries the same sense as לא תכחשו ולא תשקרו (Leviticus 19:11). We find the word ענות with bet, as in שקר ענה באחיו (Deuteronomy 19:18), and without bet, as in ישמע אל ויענם (Psalms 55:20), meaning He will answer them, and like it וכאשר לא נגענוך (Genesis 26:29) — we did not touch you. And there is a false witness who is liable to death, and that is the one concerning whom it is written ועשיתם לו כאשר זמם לעשות לאחיו (Deuteronomy 19:19)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:36:26.278327707Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}